<p><b>Description</b></p>
<p>Decomposition Argument (Through-life decomposition) Parent Claim: NCSC-TAP-ThroughLife - Through-life principles Child Claim: NCSC-TAP-Life-1 - 1. Enable people to manage their risks Justification: 1. The parent claim is too broad to assess directly at implementation level. 2. The child claim captures a necessary and testable aspect of the parent claim. 3. Confidence in the parent increases when this child claim is evidenced. Assurance 2.0 rationale: This is a child-claim -&gt; argument -&gt; parent-claim structure where the argument explicitly states why decomposition is valid and how supporting evidence for the child contributes to confidence in the parent claim. <sup>[1]</sup></p>
<p><b>References</b></p>
<ol>
<li>[1] <a href="https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/collection/technology-assurance">https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/collection/technology-assurance</a> (collected 2026-03-19 17:02:53 UTC)</li>
</ol>
]]></html-annotation>
