      <status-fields>
        <status-field type="string" name="annotation"><![CDATA[Decomposition argument: NCSC-TAP-Area-5 supports NCSC-TAP-Areas

Description:
Decomposition Argument (Decomposition)

Parent Claim:
NCSC-TAP-Areas - Technology Assurance Principles - Developing a secure product

Child Claim:
NCSC-TAP-Area-5 - 5. Review and test frequently

Justification:
1. The parent claim is too broad to assess directly at implementation level.
2. The child claim captures a necessary and testable aspect of the parent claim.
3. Confidence in the parent increases when this child claim is evidenced.

Assurance 2.0 rationale:
This is a child-claim -> argument -> parent-claim structure where the argument explicitly states
why decomposition is valid and how supporting evidence for the child contributes
to confidence in the parent claim.

Source:
https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/collection/technology-assurance

Metadata:
- Seeded By: NCSC Technology Assurance
- Seeded At (UTC): 2026-03-19 17:02:53
- Type: NCSC Technology Assurance Principle]]></status-field>
