<p><b>Draft</b></p>
<pre>Confidence Score: 8 out of 10
Weakest Node: N96265808 [argument] By cross-referencing the PCB layout against the BOM and conducting an RF scan, we provide evidence that no secondary, undocumented wireless interfaces (e.g., Bluetooth/WiFi/LTE) exist on the module to leak data out-of-band.

Rationale: The argument provided is strong as it directly relates the PCB layout and BOM to an RF scan to ensure there are no unauthorized wireless interfaces that could compromise security. The evidence used for this claim is also direct, using a physical RF scan which provides reliable results. There is minimal inferential gap between the sub-claims and the parent as they all directly relate to the main claim of ensuring physical RF isolation.

Action: To further strengthen this argument, consider performing regular security audits on the module to ensure that no new unauthorized wireless interfaces are added over time.</pre>
